ctions \u2014 passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`.\"\n\n**Code Reality**:\nThe `backlog_groom()` function signature (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`, lines 2550\u20132616) defines these parameters:\n- `selector` (str, required) \u2014 Item selector (issue #, URL, title substring, or nanoid)\n- `section` (str | None, optional) \u2014 Section name for incremental update\n- `content` (str | None, optional) \u2014 Content for the named section\n- `entry_id` (str | None, optional) \u2014 ID of entry to replace\n- `replace_section` (bool, optional) \u2014 Strike all entries and append new\n- `reason` (str | None, optional) \u2014 Reason for striking\n- `append` (bool, optional) \u2014 Append vs replace mode\n- `sections` (dict[str, str] | None, optional) \u2014 Batch section writes\n- `mark_groomed` (bool, optional) \u2014 Advance status to groomed\n\n**There is no `groomed_content` parameter.**\n\n**Evidence**:\n- File: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`\n- Lines: 2550\u20132616 (function definition)\n- Line 2618: Docstring states \"Provide section + content for section updates\" \u2014 not a single `groomed_content` blob\n\n**Impact**: HIGH\n- Users following the documentation will attempt to call `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` and receive a type-checking or runtime error\n- The pattern is misleading; the function is incremental (section-by-section), not bulk (groomed_content as a whole)\n- This affects all agents and users trying to automate item grooming\n\n**Recommendation**: \nUpdate line 5 to accurately describe the function signature:\n```\npassed through backlog_groom(selector=..., section=..., content=...)\n```\nOr broader wording:\n```\npassed through backlog_groom() using selector to identify the item, section to name the content area, and content to write or replace groomed text.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Analyzed Files\n\n**Documentation**:\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` (211 lines)\n\n**Implementation** (verification sources):\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` (BacklogItem, BacklogItemMetadata classes; status enum)\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (backlog_groom function signature and docstring)\n- `research/agent-frameworks/claude-code-harness.md` (research metadata format reference)\n\n---\n\n## Verification Method\n\n1. **Field names**: Matched against `BacklogItem` Pydantic model definition\n2. **Status values**: Cross-referenced with `_VALID_STATUSES` constant\n3. **Function signature**: Inspected complete `backlog_groom()` MCP tool definition with all parameters and annotations\n4. **Docstring alignment**: Checked function docstring vs parameter list for consistency\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe documentation is substantially accurate and aligned with implementation. The single HIGH-severity drift item (incorrect `groomed_content` parameter) is isolated to one sentence on line 5 and is correctable with a one-line update. All field names, status enums, and structural claims are verified against current HEAD commit.\n\n**Recommendation**: Merge the fix to line 5 (parameter reference) and close this audit as resolved.\n"}